      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Grid-Scale Renewable Infrastructure\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Grid-scale solar installations typically range from 1 MW to over 100 MW in capacity, with utility-scale projects commonly exceeding 50 MW\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy21osti/80694.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Energy storage systems, particularly battery storage (lithium-ion), are increasingly paired with renewable installations to address intermittency, with global battery storage capacity reaching over 14 GWh by 2023\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/battery-2023\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Wind farms typically require 2-4 acres of land per megawatt of capacity, with modern turbines rated at 10-15 MW\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/wind-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Grid modernization investments in the U.S. exceeded $50 billion annually as of 2023 to support renewable energy integration\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/lpo\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Smart grid technologies and demand response systems can reduce peak electricity demand by 5-15% when properly implemented\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/research/projects/demand-response-and-smart-grid.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global renewable energy generation capacity additions in 2023 reached approximately 295 GW, with solar and wind accounting for over 90% of new capacity\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/renewable-capacity-statistics-2024\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Transmission line constraints remain a significant bottleneck for renewable deployment, with approvals for new high-voltage lines taking 5-10 years\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/building-out-electric-grid\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Grid-scale pumped hydro storage accounts for approximately 94% of global energy storage capacity, with over 150 GW installed worldwide\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/pumped-hydro-storage\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
