    {
      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Concentrated Solar Power (CSP) and Heliostat Technology\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Concentrated Solar Power (CSP) uses mirrors or lenses to concentrate sunlight onto a small area to generate heat, which is then used to drive turbines for electricity generation\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy14ost_csp.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Heliostats are mirror systems that track the sun's position and reflect sunlight onto a central receiver (tower) or other focal point, with each heliostat containing multiple mirror segments\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar/concentrating-solar-power\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"CSP plants with thermal storage can store heat in molten salt or other media, allowing electricity generation after sunset, providing dispatchable renewable power\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2022/Jan/Renewable-Capacity-Statistics-2022\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Major CSP technologies include parabolic troughs, solar towers with heliostats, linear Fresnel reflectors, and dish systems, with solar towers being the most efficient at around 20-24% net efficiency\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/csp/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"As of 2023, global CSP capacity reached approximately 6.3 GW, with significant installations in Spain, Morocco, China, and the Middle East\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/statistics/Statistics-Time-Series\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Heliostat costs have decreased significantly, with modern heliostats costing between $100-200 per square meter of mirror area, down from over $300 per square meter a decade ago\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy19osti/72803.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The Ivanpah Solar Electric Generating System in California uses approximately 173,500 heliostats spread across 3,600 acres and produces 392 MW of electricity\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/ivanpah-solar-electric-generating-system\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Advanced heliostat designs now incorporate individual mirror segment control, adaptive optics, and automated cleaning systems to improve performance and reduce dust-related losses\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/csp/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"CSP plants require direct normal irradiance (DNI) of at least 1,500-2,000 kWh/m\u00b2/year to be economically viable, limiting deployment primarily to arid and semi-arid regions\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2018/Oct/Concentrating-Solar-Power-Technology-Brief\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The CRESOL project in Spain demonstrated a 50 MW heliostat-based solar tower with thermal storage capability, achieving a solar-to-electric efficiency of approximately 20%\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/csp/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
