      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Hybrid Renewable Systems and Integration\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hybrid renewable systems combine two or more renewable energy sources (such as solar, wind, hydro, and biomass) with energy storage to provide reliable and continuous power supply\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.int/publications/2015/Jun/Renewable-Energy-Integration-in-Power-Grids\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar-wind hybrid systems are among the most common configurations, as solar and wind resources are often complementary with wind being stronger at night and in winter while solar peaks during day and summer\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy20osti/75005.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Battery energy storage systems (BESS) are critical components in hybrid renewable systems, with lithium-ion batteries currently dominating the market at approximately 90% of installed capacity\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/batteries-and-secure-energy-transitions\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hybrid renewable systems can reduce the levelized cost of electricity (LCOE) by 20-30% compared to single-source renewable installations through improved capacity utilization and reduced storage requirements\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.int/publications/2022/Jan/Renewable-Power-Generation-Costs-in-2021\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Grid integration of hybrid renewable systems requires advanced forecasting tools, smart grid technologies, and demand-side management to maintain grid stability and balance supply with variable generation\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy19osti/72457.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"As of 2023, hybrid renewable energy projects represent approximately 15-20% of new renewable energy capacity additions globally, with significant growth projected through 2030\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/renewables-2023\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Microgrids based on hybrid renewable systems with local storage can provide energy resilience and reduce transmission losses, particularly beneficial for remote or island communities\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy20osti/76568.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Power electronics and inverter technology are essential for managing power flow between multiple renewable sources and storage systems in hybrid configurations\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.ieee.org/content/dam/ieee-org/ieee/web/org/about/corporate-partnerships/renewable-energy-integration.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
