      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Solar Energy (Photovoltaic and Thermal)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Photovoltaic (PV) cells convert sunlight directly into electricity through the photovoltaic effect, where photons knock electrons loose from atoms, creating an electric current.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar thermal systems capture heat from the sun using collectors to provide hot water and space heating, with applications ranging from residential to industrial uses.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar/solar-thermal-systems\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global solar PV capacity reached approximately 1,400 GW in 2023, with solar representing the fastest-growing renewable energy source worldwide.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Silicon-based photovoltaic cells account for approximately 95% of the market share in commercial solar panels, with monocrystalline and polycrystalline being the dominant types.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The typical efficiency of commercial photovoltaic panels ranges from 15-22%, while laboratory prototypes have achieved efficiencies exceeding 40% using multi-junction cells.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/cell-efficiency.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar thermal collectors are categorized as flat-plate collectors, evacuated tube collectors, and concentrating collectors, each suited for different temperature requirements.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar/solar-thermal-systems\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The cost of solar PV modules has decreased by approximately 90% over the past decade (2013-2023), making solar one of the cheapest electricity generation sources in many regions.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2023-Nov/Renewable-Cost-Database\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells represent an emerging technology with potential efficiencies of 20-25% and lower production costs compared to traditional silicon cells, currently in development and commercialization phases.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/perovskite-solar-cells.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar thermal systems can achieve seasonal thermal energy storage, allowing heat captured during summer months to be used for space heating and hot water during winter.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar/solar-thermal-systems\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Concentrated Solar Power (CSP) systems use mirrors and lenses to concentrate sunlight, achieving temperatures high enough for electricity generation through thermal turbines, with commercial installations reaching 10-390 MW capacity.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/csp/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
