      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Emerging Technologies (Hydrogen Fuel, Fusion, Advanced Solar)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Green hydrogen production via electrolysis using renewable electricity is considered a key pathway for decarbonization in hard-to-abate sectors such as heavy industry and long-distance transport, though current production costs remain 2-3 times higher than grey hydrogen.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/hydrogen\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Nuclear fusion has achieved significant milestones including net energy gain demonstrations, with the National Ignition Facility achieving fusion ignition in December 2022, though commercial fusion power plants remain 20-30 years away from deployment.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/national-ignition-facility-achieves-fusion-ignition\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells have demonstrated laboratory efficiencies exceeding 33% and are considered a promising complementary technology to silicon solar cells, though stability and manufacturing scalability remain active research challenges.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/cell-efficiency.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hydrogen fuel cell vehicles have limited commercial deployment with fewer than 50,000 units on roads globally, primarily constrained by lack of hydrogen refueling infrastructure and high vehicle costs.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/hydrogen-fuel-cell-vehicles\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Advanced solar technologies including bifacial panels, building-integrated photovoltaics (BIPV), and solar-thermal hybrid systems are emerging market segments with growth rates exceeding 15% annually.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/technology-roadmap-solar-photovoltaic-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hydrogen production via electrolysis currently accounts for less than 1% of global hydrogen output, with 95% derived from fossil fuels (steam methane reforming and coal gasification).\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/hydrogen\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Inertial confinement and magnetic confinement are the two primary fusion approaches being pursued commercially, with companies like Commonwealth Fusion Systems and TAE Technologies receiving significant private investment ($2+ billion combined).\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/science/doe-fusion-energy-sciences\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Tandem solar cells combining perovskite with silicon demonstrate potential efficiencies above 30%, representing a viable pathway to exceed single-junction silicon cell theoretical limits.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/perovskite-silicon-tandem-cells.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hydrogen transport and storage via pipelines, liquid hydrogen, and ammonia carriers face technical and economic challenges that currently limit large-scale deployment across energy grids.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/hydrogen\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global silicon photovoltaic cell efficiency records have plateaued near 22-23% under standard test conditions, driving investment into multi-junction and advanced materials approaches.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/cell-efficiency.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
