      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Renewable Energy Forecasting and Optimization\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar irradiance forecasting is critical for grid integration and typically uses machine learning methods including artificial neural networks, support vector machines, and ensemble techniques with accuracy improvements of 10-30% over persistence models\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rser.2015.12.314\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Wind power forecasting accuracy varies by time horizon: very short-term (0-6 hours) achieves 5-10% MAPE, short-term (6-24 hours) achieves 10-20% MAPE, and medium-term (1-7 days) achieves 15-25% MAPE using modern ensemble methods\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rser.2016.10.050\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Real-time optimization of renewable energy systems requires predictive control strategies that integrate weather forecasts with energy demand forecasting to minimize grid imbalance costs and maintain reliability\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apenergy.2018.02.003\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Deep learning architectures such as LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory) networks and convolutional neural networks have demonstrated superior performance for multi-step ahead renewable energy forecasting compared to traditional statistical methods\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apenergy.2019.113445\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Battery energy storage systems (BESS) optimization combined with renewable forecasting can reduce energy curtailment by 15-40% and improve grid stability through load leveling and frequency regulation\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apenergy.2017.11.098\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hybrid forecasting models that combine numerical weather prediction (NWP) data with statistical learning methods outperform single-method approaches by 8-15% for solar and wind power prediction\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apenergy.2020.114667\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Probabilistic forecasting using quantile regression and ensemble methods provides uncertainty quantification essential for operational decision-making in renewable-dominant grids\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijforecast.2019.05.020\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Optimal sizing and placement of distributed renewable resources can be determined through mixed-integer linear programming and genetic algorithms, reducing system costs by 20-30% compared to standard approaches\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apenergy.2019.113445\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Smart grid technologies incorporating automated demand response and microgrid control systems improve renewable energy utilization rates from 70-80% to 90-95% through real-time optimization\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apenergy.2018.07.031\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Multi-objective optimization frameworks balancing economic costs, environmental impact, and grid reliability are increasingly used for long-term renewable energy portfolio planning at regional scales\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rser.2020.110316\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
