      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Small Modular Renewable Systems (Micro-hydro, Small Wind)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Micro-hydro systems can generate between 5 kW to 100 kW of electricity and are suitable for remote locations with consistent water flow, requiring minimal civil works compared to large hydroelectric installations\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2020/Dec/Renewable-energy-integration-in-countries-of-the-Eastern-Europe-Caucasus-and-Central-Asia\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Small wind turbines typically range from 1 kW to 50 kW in capacity and can be installed on individual properties, farms, or communities to supplement grid electricity or operate off-grid\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/wind-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Micro-hydro installations have lower environmental impact than large dams as they do not require reservoir creation and can maintain natural river flow patterns\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.renewableenergyworld.com/storage/article/52921-the-pros-and-cons-of-micro-hydro-power\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Small wind turbines require average wind speeds of at least 10 mph (4.47 m/s) to be economically viable, with optimal performance at 12-14 mph average speeds\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/articles/small-wind-electric-systems\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Micro-hydro systems have typical lifespans of 20-50 years with minimal maintenance requirements, making them cost-effective for long-term energy generation\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.icimods.org/micro-hydro\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Small wind turbines have installation costs ranging from $3,000 to $8,000 per kW installed capacity as of 2023, with potential return on investment in 6-15 years depending on location and incentives\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/articles/small-wind-electric-systems\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Permitting requirements for micro-hydro installations vary significantly by region and include environmental assessments, water rights documentation, and civil engineering approvals\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.microhydropower.net/regulations\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Small wind and micro-hydro systems can be integrated with battery storage systems to provide reliable power in off-grid applications and during low generation periods\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy20osti/75703.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global small wind capacity reached approximately 1.5 GW by 2022, with growing markets in Asia, Europe, and North America driven by increasing energy independence and rural electrification needs\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://gwec.net/global-wind-report-2023/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Micro-hydro systems are particularly effective in mountainous and hilly regions with year-round water availability, making them ideal for developing countries and remote communities\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/newsroom/articles/2021/Jul/Small-scale-hydro-power-an-underestimated-resource\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
