  "content": [
    {
      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Materials Science for Renewable Energy (Perovskite, Organic PV, High-Temperature Materials)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells have achieved laboratory power conversion efficiencies exceeding 25%, with some certified results reaching 26%, making them competitive with crystalline silicon solar cells.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-021-00900-2\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Halide perovskites demonstrate hysteresis effects in current-voltage curves due to ion migration and ferroelectric polarization, which affects reproducibility of efficiency measurements.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1369702115300516\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Organic photovoltaic (OPV) cells based on non-fullerene acceptors have achieved power conversion efficiencies above 18% in single-junction devices, surpassing earlier fullerene-based systems.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41563-020-0855-x\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite stability remains a critical challenge, with degradation occurring through moisture absorption, thermal decomposition, and UV-induced ion migration, affecting commercial viability.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1364032120306876\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Lead-free perovskite alternatives such as tin-based and bismuth-based perovskites are being developed to address toxicity concerns, though with current efficiency trade-offs.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-019-0446-7\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Tandem solar cells combining perovskite top layers with crystalline silicon bottom layers have demonstrated efficiencies exceeding 29%, promising pathways beyond single-junction silicon limits.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-020-0677-7\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Ceramic matrix composites (CMCs) and single-crystal superalloys are primary high-temperature materials used in turbine blades for concentrating solar power and fossil fuel power plants, operating at temperatures above 1200\u00b0C.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360319919330216\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Organic photovoltaic cells utilize donor-acceptor bulk heterojunction architectures where phase separation and domain size critically influence exciton dissociation and charge transport.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/nphoton.2012.236\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Bandgap engineering through composition variation in ABX3 perovskites (where A, B, X are different elements) allows tuning of optical properties from ultraviolet to near-infrared regions.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1369702115000930\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Additive manufacturing techniques for high-temperature materials enable creation of complex geometries for renewable energy applications, though thermal cycling degradation remains problematic.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0001868621001774\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Graphene, carbon nanotubes, and other carbon-based nanomaterials are being integrated into perovskite and organic photovoltaic devices to improve charge transport and reduce recombination losses.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-021-23091-2\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite quantum dots exhibit quantum confinement effects enabling bandgap tuning and enhanced optical properties for specialized photovoltaic and optoelectronic applications.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0927796X20300935\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Molybdenum and tungsten oxides/disulfides are emerging as efficient hole transport and electron transport layers in perovskite devices, improving stability and performance.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41563-019-0435-0\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Environmental barrier coatings (EBCs) based on rare-earth silicates protect ceramic matrix composites in high-temperature renewable energy systems from oxidation and recession damage.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360319921001919\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Ion-exchange and cation substitution strategies in perovskites (using potassium, cesium, formamidinium, and methylammonium) improve phase stability and reduce phase segregation in mixed-halide systems.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-020-0677-7\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
