      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Energy storage systems\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Lithium-ion batteries are currently the dominant technology for energy storage, accounting for over 90% of global battery storage capacity due to their high energy density and decreasing costs\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/battery-storage\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Pumped-storage hydroelectricity remains the largest form of energy storage globally, representing approximately 90% of total installed energy storage capacity in terms of power output\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2017/Apr/Electricity-storage-and-renewables\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Energy storage systems are critical for grid stability and reliability as renewable energy sources like wind and solar are intermittent in nature\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy19osti/73222.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Battery storage costs have declined by approximately 89% between 2010 and 2020, making energy storage increasingly economically viable for grid applications\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2021/Jun/Renewable-capacity-statistics-2021\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Emerging storage technologies include solid-state batteries, flow batteries, compressed air energy storage, and thermal energy storage systems\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-018-0107-2\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Thermal energy storage systems can store heat or cold for later use and are particularly valuable for industrial processes and building climate control\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2013/Jun/Thermal-Energy-Storage\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Vanadium redox flow batteries offer advantages for long-duration storage due to their scalable design and decoupling of power and energy capacity\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306261919315722\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Grid-scale energy storage deployment is expected to grow significantly, with projections suggesting annual additions could reach 200-300 GW by 2030\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/global-energy-storage-database\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
