      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Electric vehicles and transportation\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global electric vehicle sales reached approximately 14 million units in 2023, representing about 18% of total vehicle sales worldwide, up from 9% in 2022\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/electric-vehicles\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Electric vehicles produce zero direct tailpipe emissions, significantly reducing greenhouse gas emissions compared to internal combustion engine vehicles over their lifetime\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/electric-vehicles\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Battery electric vehicles (BEVs) typically have a range of 200-300 miles per charge with modern lithium-ion batteries, though some premium models exceed 400 miles\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.fueleconomy.gov/feg/evtech.shtml\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The cost of EV batteries has decreased by approximately 90% since 2010, from around $1,100 per kWh to about $130 per kWh in 2023\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/lithium-ion-battery-costs-have-fallen-by-90-in-a-decade\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"China leads global EV adoption with over 60% of worldwide electric vehicle sales in 2023\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/electric-vehicles\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Electric vehicles charged with renewable energy sources like solar and wind provide substantially greater environmental benefits than those charged from coal or natural gas grids\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.epa.gov/greenvehicles/electric-vehicle-myths\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Most EV battery recycling programs can recover 90-95% of valuable materials including lithium, cobalt, and nickel for reuse in new batteries\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/battery-recycling-and-second-life\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Public charging infrastructure has expanded significantly, with over 1 million public charging points estimated globally as of 2023\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/global-ev-data-explorer\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
