      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Solar energy (photovoltaic and thermal)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Photovoltaic (PV) cells convert sunlight directly into electricity through the photovoltaic effect, where photons knock electrons loose from atoms in silicon or other semiconductor materials\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar/photovoltaics-how-do-photovoltaic-cells-work\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar thermal systems use sunlight to heat water or air directly for space heating, water heating, and industrial processes, with efficiencies typically ranging from 50-90%\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar/solar-thermal-systems\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global solar photovoltaic capacity reached approximately 1,500 GW by 2023, with solar becoming the fastest-growing renewable energy source\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/news/solar-pv-global-capacity-to-double-by-2029-2\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Modern residential solar panel efficiency typically ranges from 15-22%, while commercial and research-grade panels can achieve 22-50% efficiency\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/cell-efficiency.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The levelized cost of electricity (LCOE) from utility-scale solar PV has declined by approximately 90% since 2010, making it one of the cheapest electricity sources\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2023-01/Renewable-Capacity-Statistics-2023\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Concentrated Solar Power (CSP) systems use mirrors to concentrate sunlight to generate heat that drives turbines, typically achieving 15-25% efficiency\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/solar/concentrating-solar-power-technology\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"China leads global solar PV production and installation capacity, accounting for approximately 80% of global solar panel manufacturing as of 2023\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/solar-pv-global-supply-chains\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar energy systems produce 40-50 times more energy over their lifetime than is required to manufacture them, with typical lifespan of 25-30 years\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/what-is-pv-module-recycling.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
