      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Wave and ocean energy\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Wave energy converters are devices that capture energy from ocean surface waves, with potential to generate electricity at conversion rates of 2-3 kW per meter of wave front.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/marine-and-hydrokinetic-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Tidal energy harnesses the kinetic and potential energy from tides, which are highly predictable and occur with regular patterns twice per lunar day.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/marine-and-hydrokinetic-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global ocean energy resource potential is estimated at over 29,000 TWh annually from waves and tides, making it a significant untapped renewable resource.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.int/publications/2023-oct/grid-integration-of-ocean-energy-technologies\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Common wave energy device types include point absorbers, attenuators, and oscillating water columns, each with different mechanical designs for energy capture.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/marine-and-hydrokinetic-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Tidal stream generators operate similarly to wind turbines but are placed underwater to harness tidal currents, with higher energy density than wind due to water's greater mass.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/marine-and-hydrokinetic-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"As of 2024, wave and tidal energy technologies remain largely in pilot and demonstration phases, with limited commercial deployment compared to wind and solar.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/ocean-energy-technology-roadmap\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Key challenges for ocean energy development include high capital costs, harsh marine environments, environmental impact assessment, and grid integration complexities.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/marine-and-hydrokinetic-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The European Union and United Kingdom have invested heavily in wave and tidal energy projects, with several operational demonstration sites in Scotland, Portugal, and France.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.int/newsroom/pressreleases/2023/nov/renewable-capacity-growth-accelerates-globally\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
