      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Materials science for renewables\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells have achieved power conversion efficiencies exceeding 33% in laboratory settings, making them a leading contender to complement or replace silicon-based photovoltaics\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-023-01235-6\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solid-state batteries using ceramic or polymer electrolytes can potentially achieve energy densities above 400 Wh/kg, compared to 250 Wh/kg for conventional lithium-ion batteries\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2405829723000752\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"High-entropy alloys (HEAs) are being developed for applications in wind turbine gearboxes and offshore structures due to superior strength-to-weight ratios and corrosion resistance\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0079642523000191\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Graphene and carbon nanotube composites are being integrated into wind turbine blades to reduce weight while maintaining structural integrity, potentially increasing blade length and efficiency\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.compositesworld.com/articles/graphene-reinforced-composites-for-wind-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Metal halide perovskites show promise for tandem solar cells when combined with silicon, with prototype efficiencies reaching 31-32%\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.cell.com/joule/fulltext/S2542-4351(22)00416-X\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Advanced ceramic materials such as yttria-stabilized zirconia (YSZ) are critical for solid oxide fuel cells (SOFCs), operating at temperatures above 700\u00b0C with electrical efficiencies near 60%\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0008622322005693\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Organic photovoltaic (OPV) materials including non-fullerene acceptors have achieved power conversion efficiencies of 19% with improved stability over recent years\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.chemrev.3c00128\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Two-dimensional transition metal dichalcogenides (TMDs) are being investigated as cocatalysts for hydrogen generation through water splitting, with promising electrocatalytic activity\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0926337323005398\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
