      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Energy efficiency and conservation\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Energy efficiency improvements can reduce global energy demand by up to 40% by 2040, according to the International Energy Agency (IEA), making it one of the most cost-effective ways to meet energy needs.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/topics/energy-efficiency\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"LED lighting uses approximately 75% less energy than incandescent bulbs and lasts 25-50 times longer, making it a major energy conservation technology in residential and commercial buildings.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/energysaver/led-lighting\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Building energy efficiency standards and retrofits can reduce operational carbon emissions by 50-90% depending on the technology combination and building type.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/buildings\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Smart thermostats and HVAC optimization can reduce heating and cooling energy consumption by 10-23% in residential buildings.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/energysaver/thermostats\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Industrial energy efficiency improvements through better motors, compressed air systems, and process optimization can reduce industrial energy use by 20-30%.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/industry\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Energy conservation in transportation through vehicle efficiency standards and electric vehicle adoption is essential to meeting climate goals, with transportation accounting for approximately 27% of global energy-related CO2 emissions.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/topics/transport\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Insulation improvements, particularly in walls and attics, can reduce heating and cooling losses by 15-20% in residential buildings, with payback periods typically ranging from 2-8 years.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/energysaver/insulation\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Water heating represents approximately 17-25% of residential energy consumption, and energy-efficient water heaters and hot water conservation can significantly reduce overall household energy use.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/energysaver/water-heating\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
