      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Grid integration and smart grids\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Smart grids use digital communication technology to detect and react to local changes in usage, enabling two-way communication between utilities and consumers\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/energysaver/smart-grid\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Grid integration of renewable energy requires advanced forecasting, energy storage systems, and demand response mechanisms to balance variable generation from wind and solar\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy13osti/56909.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The global smart grid market was valued at approximately $36.7 billion in 2022 and is expected to grow at a CAGR of 17.9% from 2023 to 2030\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.grandviewresearch.com/industry-analysis/smart-grid-market\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Smart grids can reduce peak demand by 5-15% through demand response and load management programs\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/smart-grids\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Microgrids are localized networks within smart grids that can operate independently and help integrate distributed renewable energy sources like rooftop solar\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/energysaver/microgrids\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Battery energy storage systems (BESS) are critical for smart grids to store excess renewable energy and discharge it during peak demand periods\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2017/Oct/Renewable-Energy-Integration-in-Power-Grids\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The US invested approximately $3.5 billion in grid modernization through the Bipartisan Infrastructure Law to support smart grid deployment\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/biden-harris-administration-and-congress-advance-clean-energy-jobs-and-environmental-justice-through\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Advanced metering infrastructure (AMI) enables real-time monitoring of electricity consumption, which is a foundational component of smart grids\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.eia.gov/tools/faqs/faq.php?id=108&t=3\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Grid-connected renewable energy sources accounted for over 12% of global electricity generation in 2021, with smart grid technology essential for managing this integration\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2022/Apr/Renewable-Energy-Statistics-2022\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Phasor Measurement Units (PMUs) provide real-time data on grid voltage and frequency, enabling faster detection and response to grid disturbances in smart grids\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.ieee.org/content/dam/ieee-org/ieee/web/standards/standards_icc_1.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
