      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Circular economy and recycling in renewable energy\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar panel recycling can recover up to 95% of glass and 85% of silicon, with emerging technologies enabling recovery of valuable materials like aluminum frames and junction boxes\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2016/Jun/End-of-life-management-Solar-Photovoltaic-Panels\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Wind turbine blades present a circular economy challenge, with approximately 43 million tons of blade waste expected by 2050 globally, though recycling methods are being developed using mechanical and chemical processes\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2019/Sep/Waste-and-Circular-Economy-in-the-Renewable-Energy-Sector\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Battery recycling from renewable energy storage systems can recover lithium, cobalt, nickel, and other critical materials, with recycling recovery rates now reaching 90-95% for lithium-ion batteries\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/batteries-and-recycling\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The European Union's Circular Economy Action Plan includes extended producer responsibility requirements for renewable energy equipment manufacturers to promote material recovery and recycling\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://ec.europa.eu/environment/circular-economy/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Recycled materials from renewable energy systems can reduce manufacturing emissions by 20-50% compared to virgin material extraction for solar panels, wind turbines, and battery components\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2016/Jun/End-of-life-management-Solar-Photovoltaic-Panels\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Currently only about 5-10% of end-of-life solar panels globally are recycled, creating significant opportunities for circular economy development in the renewable energy sector\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/newsroom/articles/2021/Jun/Solar-panel-recycling\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Critical minerals required for renewable energy technologies (rare earths, cobalt, lithium) have increased recycling targets under circular economy initiatives to reduce supply chain vulnerabilities\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/critical-minerals-in-clean-energy-transitions\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hydroelectric turbine components and geothermal equipment have higher recycling rates (70-90%) compared to solar and wind due to longer established metal recycling infrastructure\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2019/Sep/Waste-and-Circular-Economy-in-the-Renewable-Energy-Sector\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
