      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Environmental and social impacts of renewables\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Renewable energy technologies have significantly lower lifecycle greenhouse gas emissions compared to fossil fuels, with solar PV and wind producing 10-48 times less CO2 per unit of energy over their lifetime\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.ipcc.ch/report/ar6/wg3/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar and wind installations require substantial land areas, with potential impacts on ecosystems, though lifecycle land use per energy unit is lower than fossil fuel extraction areas\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-017-0035-6\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Wind turbines can negatively impact bird and bat populations through collision and habitat disruption, though total mortality is lower than impacts from fossil fuel infrastructure and other human activities\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.fws.gov/birds/bird-topics/energy-development/wind-turbines.php\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Renewable energy manufacturing, particularly solar panels and batteries, involves mining critical minerals (lithium, cobalt, rare earths) with associated environmental and human rights concerns\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/the-role-of-critical-minerals-in-clean-energy-transitions\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Renewable energy expansion can create employment opportunities and energy independence benefits, particularly in rural areas where wind and solar farms are developed\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy19osti/72362.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hydroelectric dams create ecological impacts through altered water flows, fish migration barriers, and methane emissions from reservoirs, though benefits vary by site characteristics\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-021-24029-4\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Energy transition from fossil fuels to renewables can reduce air pollution-related health impacts, preventing millions of premature deaths from improved air quality\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.thelancet.com/commissions/climate-change\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Renewable energy development can raise land use conflicts with indigenous communities and agricultural areas, requiring careful siting and community engagement strategies\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.undp.org/sites/g/files/zskgf546/files/documents/UNDP-biofuels-indigenous-eng.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Battery storage for renewables involves environmental costs in lithium and cobalt extraction, though recycling technologies are improving to reduce new mining demands\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/battery-recycling-for-electric-vehicles\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Offshore wind installations have localized marine ecosystem impacts during construction and operation, but evidence shows marine life adaptation in many established offshore wind farms\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fmars.2019.00253/full\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
