      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Emerging technologies (perovskites, organic solar cells)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells have achieved laboratory power conversion efficiencies exceeding 25%, with some reports reaching 33.5% in tandem configurations, rivaling traditional crystalline silicon cells.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-022-01012-z\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskites are typically made from a combination of organic and inorganic materials arranged in an ABX3 crystal structure, most commonly methylammonium lead iodide (MAPbI3) or formamidinium-based compositions.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360319921006455\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Organic solar cells (OSCs) currently achieve power conversion efficiencies around 18-19% in single-junction devices and have demonstrated over 20% in tandem configurations using non-fullerene acceptors.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/adma.202207288\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Stability and degradation remain major challenges for perovskite solar cells, with moisture, heat, and light exposure causing rapid performance loss, though encapsulation and compositional engineering approaches show promise.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-020-00721-5\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Organic solar cells demonstrate excellent light absorption properties and can be processed using solution-based methods such as spin-coating and roll-to-roll printing, enabling low-cost manufacturing.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2211379721003867\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Lead toxicity in perovskite solar cells is a significant environmental and health concern, spurring research into lead-free alternatives such as tin-based, germanium-based, and double-perovskite compounds.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acsenergylett.1c00915\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Tandem perovskite-silicon solar cells have achieved efficiencies exceeding 32%, demonstrating the potential for combining perovskites with established silicon technology.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-021-00953-z\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Non-fullerene acceptors (NFAs) have become the dominant electron acceptor material in organic solar cells, replacing earlier fullerene-based designs due to superior performance and tunability.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/advs.202005689\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells can be manufactured at lower temperatures (150-200\u00b0C) compared to silicon solar cells (800-1000\u00b0C), reducing production energy costs.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/nature12373\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Operational stability testing of organic solar cells has shown degradation rates improving significantly, with some devices maintaining over 90% of initial efficiency after 10,000 hours under controlled conditions.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2211379720308846\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells can be manufactured in flexible form, enabling lightweight and bendable photovoltaic applications compared to rigid silicon alternatives.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.nanolett.1c04557\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Grain boundary engineering and defect passivation in perovskites have emerged as key strategies to improve efficiency and stability by reducing non-radiative recombination losses.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-021-00943-z\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Organic solar cells exhibit narrow bandgaps compared to perovskites, allowing for better utilization of the near-infrared portion of the solar spectrum but generally lower voltages.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2211379721001849\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Commercialization efforts for perovskite solar cells are underway, with several companies targeting module production in the near term, though substantial scale-up challenges remain.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-022-01050-5\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Inverted perovskite architectures (p-i-n configuration) have shown improved stability and performance compared to conventional n-i-p designs in some applications.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acsenergylett.0c01623\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
