      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Energy efficiency and demand management\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Energy efficiency improvements can reduce global energy demand by approximately 40% by 2040, making it one of the most cost-effective ways to meet energy needs alongside renewable energy expansion.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/topics/energy-efficiency\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Smart meters and advanced metering infrastructure (AMI) enable real-time monitoring of energy consumption and help reduce peak demand by 5-15% through demand response programs.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/smart-manufacturing-and-industrial-efficiency\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Demand-side management (DSM) programs can integrate renewable energy sources more effectively by shifting consumption patterns to match generation from wind and solar resources.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/grid-modernization/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Building energy efficiency improvements account for approximately 30% of the cost-effective emissions reduction potential needed to meet climate targets.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/buildings\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Demand response programs can provide 50-100 GW of flexible load capacity in developed economies, supporting grid stability with renewable energy integration.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/how-demand-response-supports-grid-flexibility\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"LED lighting upgrades can reduce lighting energy consumption by 75% compared to incandescent bulbs and represent one of the quickest energy efficiency wins.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/led-basics\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Industrial energy efficiency measures can reduce energy consumption by 20-30% through process optimization, waste heat recovery, and variable speed drives.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/energy-efficiency\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Time-of-use (TOU) pricing structures incentivize consumers to shift electricity consumption away from peak hours, reducing strain on grid infrastructure.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/demand-side-management\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
