      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Solar energy (photovoltaic and thermal)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Photovoltaic (PV) cells convert sunlight directly into electricity through the photovoltaic effect, while solar thermal systems use sunlight to heat water or air for heating and hot water applications\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/research/re-photovoltaics.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global solar PV capacity reached approximately 1,414 GW by the end of 2023, with solar being the fastest-growing renewable energy source\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/solar-pv-global-supply-chains\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Silicon-based solar cells account for approximately 95% of the current photovoltaic market, with crystalline silicon technology being the dominant type\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/cell-efficiency.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Modern commercial solar PV panels typically have efficiencies ranging from 15-22%, with laboratory prototypes achieving efficiencies above 40% using multi-junction cells\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/cell-efficiency.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar thermal systems can achieve efficiency rates of 50-80% for heating applications, making them more efficient than PV for direct heating purposes\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/solar\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The global weighted-average cost of electricity from utility-scale solar PV declined by 89% between 2010 and 2020, making solar one of the cheapest electricity sources\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2021-Jun/Renewable-cost-and-competitiveness\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells are emerging as a promising next-generation technology with potential efficiencies exceeding 30% and lower manufacturing costs than silicon-based cells\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/perovskite-solar-cells.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solar thermal systems are particularly effective for space heating, pool heating, and domestic hot water applications in residential and commercial buildings\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/solar\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Concentrated solar power (CSP) systems use mirrors or lenses to concentrate sunlight and generate heat that drives turbines for electricity generation, with some systems incorporating thermal storage\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/csp/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"China dominates global solar manufacturing with approximately 80% of polysilicon production and over 70% of solar panel manufacturing capacity as of 2023\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/solar-pv-global-supply-chains\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
