      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Energy storage systems and batteries\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Lithium-ion batteries dominate the energy storage market, accounting for over 90% of global battery storage capacity as of 2023-2024\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/energy-system/energy-storage\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Battery energy storage systems (BESS) have experienced a compound annual growth rate of over 30% between 2017-2023, with global capacity reaching over 16 GW in 2023\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.statista.com/outlook/cmo/energy-storage-systems/worldwide\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solid-state batteries are emerging as a next-generation technology with higher energy density and faster charging capabilities compared to current lithium-ion batteries\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/news/program/2024/solid-state-battery-research.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Pumped hydroelectric storage remains the largest form of energy storage globally by capacity, representing approximately 90% of all utility-scale storage\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/energy-storage\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Flow batteries, including vanadium redox and zinc-bromine variants, are being deployed for long-duration energy storage applications lasting 4-12 hours or more\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/long-duration-storage-shot\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The global energy storage market is projected to grow from approximately 9 GWh in 2020 to over 400 GWh annually by 2030\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.bnef.com/insights/27648\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Sodium-ion batteries are entering commercial production as a cost-effective alternative to lithium-ion batteries, particularly for stationary energy storage\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/articles/sodium-ion-battery-production\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Grid-scale battery storage systems are increasingly paired with renewable energy facilities to address intermittency issues and support grid stability\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2022/Oct/Battery-storage-technologies-for-energy-transition\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
