      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Enhanced Geothermal Systems (EGS)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Enhanced Geothermal Systems (EGS) are engineered reservoirs created in hot rock formations where natural permeability or porosity is insufficient for economic power generation, involving hydraulic stimulation to increase rock permeability\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/geothermal/enhanced-geothermal-systems\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The U.S. Department of Energy launched the Enhanced Geothermal Shot in 2022 with a goal to reduce EGS costs by 90% and develop 60 GW of deployable EGS capacity by 2050\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/biden-harris-administration-announces-enhanced-geothermal-shot-accelerate-americas\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Unlike traditional geothermal energy that requires specific geological conditions with existing hydrothermal resources, EGS technology can potentially be deployed in many locations with access to hot rock at depth\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/analysis/re-assume.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Fervo Energy achieved a significant milestone in 2023 by demonstrating commercial-scale EGS technology in Nevada with improved heat extraction and well performance compared to previous projects\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.fervoenenergy.com/news\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"EGS projects face technical challenges including induced seismicity, well completion technology, and maintaining long-term reservoir productivity and permeability\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.usgs.gov/programs/vhz/volcanic-rocks-and-geothermal-development\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The estimated global potential for EGS resources exceeds 50 exajoules of accessible heat at depths below 3 km, significantly larger than traditional geothermal potential\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/geothermal-direct-use-and-heat-pumps\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Commercial EGS deployment requires drilling technology capable of creating wells at depths of 3-5 km in crystalline basement rock with horizontal wellbore sections\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.spe.org/en/news-releases/geothermal-energy/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Several countries including Australia, Iceland, Japan, and the United Kingdom have active EGS research and demonstration projects underway\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.globalgeothermalalliance.org\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
