      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Advanced thermal storage systems\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Sensible heat thermal storage systems store energy by heating or cooling a medium such as water, molten salt, or solid materials, with storage capacity dependent on specific heat capacity and temperature change\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rser.2013.03.012\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Latent heat thermal storage using phase change materials (PCMs) can store 5-14 times more energy per unit mass than sensible heat storage systems\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rser.2018.03.087\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Molten salt thermal storage systems, particularly two-tank indirect systems using nitrate salts, can achieve storage efficiencies of 90-95% and enable 10-15 hours of thermal energy storage for concentrated solar power plants\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.solmat.2014.06.005\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Thermochemical storage systems utilizing reversible chemical reactions can achieve energy densities of 150-300 kWh/m\u00b3, significantly higher than sensible or latent heat storage\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rser.2014.07.115\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Concrete thermal storage has been demonstrated as an economical solid medium for sensible heat storage in building-integrated thermal storage systems with round-trip efficiencies of 75-85%\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apenergy.2019.113520\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Packed bed thermal storage systems using rocks or ceramics combined with air or liquid heat transfer fluids are cost-effective solutions for medium-temperature applications (200-600\u00b0C)\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.solener.2015.10.021\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Cryogenic liquid air energy storage can achieve round-trip electrical efficiencies of 50-70% and provides long-term storage with minimal self-discharge losses\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apenergy.2013.06.021\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Advanced thermal storage integration with concentrated solar power (CSP) systems extends plant operating hours from 8 to 24 hours, significantly improving capacity factors\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rser.2013.03.024\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
