  "content": [
    {
      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Hydroelectric and pumped hydro storage\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hydropower accounts for approximately 16% of global electricity generation, making it the largest source of renewable electricity worldwide\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/hydropower\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Pumped hydro storage is the most mature and widely deployed energy storage technology, accounting for over 90% of global energy storage capacity\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2021-May/Renewable-Capacity-Statistics-2021\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Pumped hydro storage systems can achieve round-trip energy efficiency of 70-85%, storing energy by pumping water to elevated reservoirs and releasing it through turbines\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/pumped-storage-hydropower\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Run-of-river hydroelectric systems generate power from flowing water without large reservoir storage, reducing environmental impact compared to traditional dam projects\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.renewablesfirst.co.uk/hydropower/hydropower-basics/run-of-river-hydro/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Global pumped hydro storage capacity reached approximately 160 GW as of 2023, with projections showing significant growth through 2030\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.icold-cigb.org/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Norway operates the world's largest pumped hydro storage facility with the Kvilldal power station and maintains extensive hydroelectric infrastructure generating nearly 100% of its electricity\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.ssb.no/en/energi-og-industri/statistikker/elektrisitet\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Hydroelectric dams can have operational lifespans exceeding 50-100 years with minimal fuel costs and low operational carbon emissions\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.hydropower.org/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Environmental concerns with large hydroelectric projects include habitat disruption, altered river flows, and methane emissions from reservoir decomposition in tropical regions\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.worldwildlife.org/threats/dams-and-water-management\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"China leads global hydropower generation capacity with over 380 GW installed, followed by Brazil, Canada, and the United States\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.hydropower.org/status-report\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Emerging pumped hydro technologies include closed-loop systems that don't require natural reservoirs and underground pumped storage facilities\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-020-00671-z\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
