  "content": [
    {
      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Renewable energy materials science and manufacturing\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells have achieved laboratory efficiencies exceeding 33% and are considered a leading next-generation photovoltaic technology due to their low manufacturing costs and tunable bandgap properties\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-021-00901-x\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Silicon remains the dominant material for commercial solar panel production, accounting for approximately 95% of the global photovoltaic market, despite emerging alternatives like perovskites and cadmium telluride\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/photovoltaic-manufacturing-costs-2021\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Solid-state batteries using lithium metal anodes and ceramic electrolytes promise energy densities above 500 Wh/kg, significantly higher than current lithium-ion batteries at 250-300 Wh/kg\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-020-0584-0\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Critical supply chain vulnerabilities exist for renewable energy manufacturing, particularly for rare earth elements used in wind turbine permanent magnets, with China controlling approximately 70% of global processing capacity\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/reports/critical-minerals-and-clean-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Bifacial solar panels, which capture sunlight on both front and rear surfaces, can achieve 10-25% higher power output compared to monofacial panels under optimal installation conditions\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy20osti/75002.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Advanced manufacturing techniques like roll-to-roll processing can reduce thin-film photovoltaic manufacturing costs by 30-50% compared to traditional batch manufacturing methods\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/advanced-manufacturing-renewable-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Tandem solar cells combining perovskite and silicon layers have demonstrated efficiencies above 30%, surpassing single-junction silicon solar cells which are theoretically limited to 29%\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.aaz3503\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Lithium extraction for battery manufacturing requires approximately 500,000 gallons of water per ton of lithium produced, raising sustainability concerns for arid regions with major lithium reserves\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/how-much-water-does-it-take-mine-lithium\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Wind turbine blade materials are transitioning from fiberglass to advanced composites including carbon fiber and bioresins to reduce weight and improve recyclability\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/wind/advanced-materials-wind-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Sodium-ion batteries are emerging as a commercial alternative to lithium-ion batteries, with CATL and other manufacturers beginning mass production due to lower costs and improved thermal stability\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.batteriesinternational.com/catl-sodium-ion-battery\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
