Message:
{
  "id": "msg_011Cf7cE9xM6zSvT2CDpd2T4",
  "container": null,
  "content": [
    {
      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Emerging technologies (floating solar, perovskite cells, etc.)\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Floating solar photovoltaic systems, also known as floatovoltaics, are installed on water bodies such as reservoirs, ponds, and lakes, and can reduce water evaporation while generating electricity\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/news/program/2021/floating-solar-could-help-two-birds-with-one-stone.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells have achieved laboratory efficiencies exceeding 30% and are considered a promising next-generation photovoltaic technology due to their lower manufacturing costs compared to silicon cells\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41560-021-00900-0\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The global floating solar market was valued at approximately $3 billion in 2022 and is expected to grow at a compound annual growth rate of over 15% through 2030\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.grandviewresearch.com/industry-analysis/floating-solar-market\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite solar cells face commercialization challenges including stability issues, lead toxicity concerns, and scaling difficulties that researchers are actively working to overcome\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1364032122007262\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Bifacial solar panels, which capture sunlight from both front and rear surfaces, can increase energy output by 10-25% compared to traditional monofacial panels\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/pv/bifacial-photovoltaics.html\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Perovskite-silicon tandem solar cells have demonstrated efficiencies above 29% in laboratory settings, showing potential to surpass conventional silicon cell efficiency limits\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.cell.com/joule/fulltext/S2542-4351(21)00253-8\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Floating solar farms can improve the performance of photovoltaic panels by 5-10% due to the cooling effect of water, which reduces operating temperatures\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0360544220322223\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"China leads global floating solar deployment with projects like the 40 MW Qinghai floating solar farm, while Singapore and Portugal are also expanding floatovoltaic installations\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2022/Jun/Floating-Solar-Market-Report\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Organic photovoltaic (OPV) cells are an emerging technology offering advantages such as flexibility, light weight, and potential for low-cost manufacturing through printing techniques\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2211285521003906\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Quantum dot solar cells represent an emerging technology with potential to achieve efficiencies over 45% theoretically, though current laboratory demonstrations remain below 20%\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fchem.2021.713374\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
