      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Renewable energy policy and incentives\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Feed-in tariffs (FITs) guarantee renewable energy producers fixed prices for electricity fed into the grid, and have been instrumental in accelerating solar and wind deployment in Germany, Spain, and other European countries.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2012/Jun/Renewable-Energy-Cost-and-Benefit-Analysis\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Investment tax credits (ITCs) and production tax credits (PTCs) in the United States have significantly reduced the cost of renewable energy deployment by allowing developers to deduct a percentage of capital costs or earn credits based on energy produced.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy21osti/80694.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Renewable Portfolio Standards (RPS) mandate that utilities source a minimum percentage of electricity from renewable sources, creating market demand and driving investment in renewable capacity.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy19osti/73263.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Net metering policies allow distributed renewable energy producers (such as rooftop solar owners) to receive credit for excess electricity they supply to the grid, improving project economics for residential and small commercial installations.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2016/Jun/Renewable-Energy-Integration-in-Power-Grids\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Renewable energy auctions have become an increasingly popular policy mechanism, with competitive bidding driving down costs; solar and wind projects have achieved record-low prices through auction-based procurement in countries including India, the UAE, and Chile.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2021/Jun/Renewable-Power-Generation-Costs-in-2021\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Subsidy removal and fossil fuel support reduction are critical policy priorities according to international energy agencies, as direct and indirect subsidies for fossil fuels globally exceed $7 trillion annually (when accounting for environmental costs), creating unequal competition with renewables.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.imf.org/en/Publications/WP/Issues/2021/09/23/Still-Not-Getting-Energy-Prices-Right-A-Global-and-Country-Assessment-of-Fossil-Fuel-Subsidies-460466\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Carbon pricing mechanisms including carbon taxes and emissions trading systems (ETS) create financial incentives for transitioning from fossil fuels to renewable energy by incorporating climate costs into energy pricing.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.icap.world/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Accelerated depreciation allowances and green bonds financing mechanisms have emerged as important policy tools to reduce capital costs and improve project financing for renewable energy infrastructure.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2017/Nov/Renewable-Energy-Financing-and-Investment\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Policies supporting energy storage integration, grid modernization, and smart grid infrastructure are increasingly recognized as essential complements to variable renewable energy deployment policies.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2017/Oct/Electricity-storage-and-renewables-costs-and-markets\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Workforce development and training incentives are increasingly included in renewable energy policies to address labor market gaps and support just transition principles in renewable energy deployment.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2021/Jan/Measuring-Socio-Economic-Impacts-of-Renewable-Energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
