      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Nuclear fusion and advanced nuclear technologies\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Nuclear fusion reactions occur when two light atomic nuclei combine to form a heavier nucleus, releasing enormous amounts of energy; this is the process powering the sun and requires temperatures exceeding 100 million Kelvin on Earth\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iter.org/sci/fusion\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The US National Ignition Facility (NIF) achieved net energy gain in December 2022, producing 3.15 megajoules of output energy from 2.05 megajoules of input laser energy, marking the first time fusion has produced more energy than was directly delivered to the fuel\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/national-ignition-facility-achieves-fusion-ignition\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Two main approaches to achieving controlled fusion are inertial confinement fusion (ICF) using high-powered lasers or particle beams, and magnetic confinement fusion using powerful magnetic fields to contain plasma\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.world-nuclear.org/information-library/current-and-future-generation/nuclear-fusion.aspx\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"ITER (International Thermonuclear Experimental Reactor) in France is a large-scale magnetic confinement fusion experiment designed to demonstrate the feasibility of fusion as a sustainable energy source, with first plasma operations expected in the late 2020s\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iter.org/\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Advanced fission technologies including Generation IV reactors and small modular reactors (SMRs) offer enhanced safety features, reduced waste production, and improved fuel efficiency compared to conventional nuclear reactors\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iaea.org/newscenter/news-stories/what-are-generation-iv-nuclear-reactors-and-why-do-we-need-them\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Private fusion companies including Commonwealth Fusion Systems, TAE Technologies, and Helion Energy are pursuing alternative fusion approaches with funding from both venture capital and government sources, targeting commercial demonstration reactors in the 2030s\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/articles/doe-announces-new-initiative-accelerate-development-fusion-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Deuterium-tritium (D-T) fuel is the primary fuel mixture used in most near-term fusion demonstration projects due to its relatively high fusion cross-section at achievable temperatures\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.world-nuclear.org/information-library/current-and-future-generation/nuclear-fusion.aspx\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Fusion energy produces minimal long-lived radioactive waste compared to fission, with activation products having half-lives measured in decades rather than thousands of years, and no chain reaction risk\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iter.org/sci/fusionfacts\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Commercial fusion power plants are not expected to contribute significantly to global electricity supply before 2050, with most projections suggesting meaningful deployment in the second half of the 21st century\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/fusion-is-set-to-play-a-key-role-in-global-energy-decarbonisation\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Advanced nuclear technologies including fast breeder reactors and thorium-based reactors could extend nuclear fuel resources and reduce long-term waste concerns, though commercial deployment remains limited\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.world-nuclear.org/information-library/nuclear-fuel-cycle/fuel-and-fission-products/thorium.aspx\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
