    {
      "citations": null,
      "text": "```json\n{\n  \"subtopic\": \"Microgrid and distributed energy systems\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Microgrids are localized groups of electricity sources, loads, and control systems that operate either connected to the main grid or independently in island mode, and can improve grid resilience and integrate renewable energy sources effectively.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy19osti/34303.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Distributed Energy Resources (DERs) including rooftop solar, battery storage, and small wind turbines enable communities to generate power locally, reducing transmission losses which can account for 5-7% of electricity in conventional centralized systems.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.eia.gov/energyexplained/index.php\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Microgrids require sophisticated control systems and communication infrastructure (often involving IoT and advanced metering) to manage power flow and maintain frequency and voltage stability, particularly during transitions between grid-connected and island modes.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.ieee.org/content/dam/ieee-org/ieee/web/standards/standards_isoiec_iec_62619_ed2_en.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Battery energy storage systems (BESS), particularly lithium-ion batteries, have become cost-competitive for microgrids, with prices declining approximately 89% between 2010 and 2020, enabling wider microgrid deployment.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.irena.org/publications/2021-Jul/Battery-Storage-Costs-Trends\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Microgrids can enhance energy independence for remote or island communities and improve disaster resilience for critical infrastructure by operating independently during grid outages.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy17osti/68773.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Regulatory and interconnection standards remain significant barriers to microgrid deployment, though standards such as IEEE 1547 and UL 4001 are being developed to address technical requirements and grid integration protocols.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.nrel.gov/docs/fy20osti/76694.pdf\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Peer-to-peer (P2P) energy trading within microgrids enabled by blockchain technology is emerging as a potential mechanism to optimize local energy distribution and create new market structures for prosumers.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0306261921002890\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"The global microgrid market was valued at approximately $5.9 billion in 2022 and is projected to grow at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 12-14% through 2030, driven by renewable integration and grid modernization policies.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.mordorintelligence.com/industry-reports/microgrid-market\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Demand response programs integrated within microgrids can reduce peak loads by 15-25% through automated load management and real-time pricing signals, enhancing overall system efficiency.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.energy.gov/eere/articles/demand-response-peak-load-reduction\",\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"fact\": \"Smart grid technologies including sensors, SCADA systems, and AI-based forecasting are essential components of modern microgrids to predict renewable generation variability and optimize dispatch decisions in real-time.\",\n      \"source_url\": \"https://www.iea.org/articles/digitalization-and-energy\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
